:Namespace Evaluation
    ⍝ Hand-crafted evaluation: material plus piece-square tables.

    ⎕IO ⎕ML←1

    ⍝ Piece values in centipawns, in the order P N B R Q K.
    VALUES←100 320 330 500 900 0

    ⍝ Piece-square tables from the Simplified Evaluation Function. Each
    ⍝ table is a bonus in centipawns for a white piece on that square,
    ⍝ laid out as the board is seen from white's side: rank 8 is the top
    ⍝ row, the a-file the left column. No entry exceeds half a pawn, so
    ⍝ placement never outweighs a piece.

    PAWN_TABLE←[
          0   0   0   0   0   0   0   0
         50  50  50  50  50  50  50  50
         10  10  20  30  30  20  10  10
          5   5  10  25  25  10   5   5
          0   0   0  20  20   0   0   0
          5  ¯5 ¯10   0   0 ¯10  ¯5   5
          5  10  10 ¯20 ¯20  10  10   5
          0   0   0   0   0   0   0   0
    ]

    KNIGHT_TABLE←[
        ¯50 ¯40 ¯30 ¯30 ¯30 ¯30 ¯40 ¯50
        ¯40 ¯20   0   0   0   0 ¯20 ¯40
        ¯30   0  10  15  15  10   0 ¯30
        ¯30   5  15  20  20  15   5 ¯30
        ¯30   0  15  20  20  15   0 ¯30
        ¯30   5  10  15  15  10   5 ¯30
        ¯40 ¯20   0   5   5   0 ¯20 ¯40
        ¯50 ¯40 ¯30 ¯30 ¯30 ¯30 ¯40 ¯50
    ]

    BISHOP_TABLE←[
        ¯20 ¯10 ¯10 ¯10 ¯10 ¯10 ¯10 ¯20
        ¯10   0   0   0   0   0   0 ¯10
        ¯10   0   5  10  10   5   0 ¯10
        ¯10   5   5  10  10   5   5 ¯10
        ¯10   0  10  10  10  10   0 ¯10
        ¯10  10  10  10  10  10  10 ¯10
        ¯10   5   0   0   0   0   5 ¯10
        ¯20 ¯10 ¯10 ¯10 ¯10 ¯10 ¯10 ¯20
    ]

    ROOK_TABLE←[
          0   0   0   0   0   0   0   0
          5  10  10  10  10  10  10   5
         ¯5   0   0   0   0   0   0  ¯5
         ¯5   0   0   0   0   0   0  ¯5
         ¯5   0   0   0   0   0   0  ¯5
         ¯5   0   0   0   0   0   0  ¯5
         ¯5   0   0   0   0   0   0  ¯5
          0   0   0   5   5   0   0   0
    ]

    QUEEN_TABLE←[
        ¯20 ¯10 ¯10  ¯5  ¯5 ¯10 ¯10 ¯20
        ¯10   0   0   0   0   0   0 ¯10
        ¯10   0   5   5   5   5   0 ¯10
         ¯5   0   5   5   5   5   0  ¯5
          0   0   5   5   5   5   0  ¯5
        ¯10   5   5   5   5   5   0 ¯10
        ¯10   0   5   0   0   0   0 ¯10
        ¯20 ¯10 ¯10  ¯5  ¯5 ¯10 ¯10 ¯20
    ]

    ⍝ Middlegame king: sheltered on the back rank behind its pawns.
    KING_MIDDLEGAME_TABLE←[
        ¯30 ¯40 ¯40 ¯50 ¯50 ¯40 ¯40 ¯30
        ¯30 ¯40 ¯40 ¯50 ¯50 ¯40 ¯40 ¯30
        ¯30 ¯40 ¯40 ¯50 ¯50 ¯40 ¯40 ¯30
        ¯30 ¯40 ¯40 ¯50 ¯50 ¯40 ¯40 ¯30
        ¯20 ¯30 ¯30 ¯40 ¯40 ¯30 ¯30 ¯20
        ¯10 ¯20 ¯20 ¯20 ¯20 ¯20 ¯20 ¯10
         20  20   0   0   0   0  20  20
         20  30  10   0   0  10  30  20
    ]

    ⍝ Endgame king: active in the centre.
    KING_ENDGAME_TABLE←[
        ¯50 ¯40 ¯30 ¯20 ¯20 ¯30 ¯40 ¯50
        ¯30 ¯20 ¯10   0   0 ¯10 ¯20 ¯30
        ¯30 ¯10  20  30  30  20 ¯10 ¯30
        ¯30 ¯10  30  40  40  30 ¯10 ¯30
        ¯30 ¯10  30  40  40  30 ¯10 ¯30
        ¯30 ¯10  20  30  30  20 ¯10 ¯30
        ¯30 ¯30   0   0   0   0 ¯30 ¯30
        ¯50 ¯30 ¯30 ¯30 ¯30 ¯30 ¯30 ¯50
    ]

    ⍝ Value of each piece type on each square, one row per type in the
    ⍝ order P N B R Q K and one column per square, a1 to h8, with the
    ⍝ middlegame king. Reversing a table's rows puts rank 1 first, as in
    ⍝ the bitboards. A black piece is worth what a white piece is worth
    ⍝ on the square reflected top to bottom, which is the table
    ⍝ unreversed.
    TABLES←PAWN_TABLE KNIGHT_TABLE BISHOP_TABLE ROOK_TABLE QUEEN_TABLE KING_MIDDLEGAME_TABLE
    WHITE_VALUES←VALUES+⍤0 1↑,∘⊖¨TABLES
    BLACK_VALUES←VALUES+⍤0 1↑,¨TABLES

    ⍝ Change in a king's value from the middlegame to the endgame table,
    ⍝ per square, a1 to h8.
    KING_SHIFT←KING_ENDGAME_TABLE-KING_MIDDLEGAME_TABLE
    WHITE_KING_SHIFT←,⊖KING_SHIFT
    BLACK_KING_SHIFT←,KING_SHIFT

    ⍝ Game phase: each piece other than pawns and kings counts towards
    ⍝ it, in the order P N B R Q K. The pieces of the start position
    ⍝ make up the full middlegame, MAX_PHASE; no pieces left is the pure
    ⍝ endgame, 0. Promotions can push the count past MAX_PHASE, so it is
    ⍝ capped there.
    PHASE_WEIGHTS←0 1 1 2 4 0
    MAX_PHASE←24

    evaluate←{
        ⍝ Score of a position from its material and piece placement.
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ bitboards, game state
        ⍝ ← ←→ score: whole centipawns from the side to move's point of
        ⍝      view

        (bitboards game_state)←⍵
        white_pieces←bitboards[##.Pieces.(P N B R Q K);]
        black_pieces←bitboards[##.Pieces.(p n b r q k);]

        ⍝ The king's value moves from the middlegame towards the endgame
        ⍝ table in proportion to the material gone, so a single trade
        ⍝ never makes the score jump.
        phase←MAX_PHASE⌊+/PHASE_WEIGHTS×+/white_pieces+black_pieces
        endgame←1-phase÷MAX_PHASE
        white←(+/,WHITE_VALUES×white_pieces)+endgame×+/WHITE_KING_SHIFT×white_pieces[6;]
        black←(+/,BLACK_VALUES×black_pieces)+endgame×+/BLACK_KING_SHIFT×black_pieces[6;]

        ⍝ white-black scores from white's point of view; the sign turns
        ⍝ that into the side to move's. Rounding half away from zero
        ⍝ gives a position and its colour-swapped mirror image the same
        ⍝ score.
        score←white-black
        sign←1-2×game_state[##.GameState.side]
        sign×(×score)×⌊0.5+|score
    }
:EndNamespace
